  "description": "DiveIndexPool is a .NET 8.0 library that seeks to provide performant, memory-efficient pools of integer indexes. DiveIndexPool offers simple, clear APIs for taking, returning, enumerating, and managing indexes. It offers multiple implementations ranging from extremely fast bitmask-based pools for small capacities up to large, scalable, and thread-safe pools for high-demand scenarios. By recycling and reusing numeric indexes, you can reduce overhead and fragmentation in scenarios such as object recycling, memory management, network connection tracking, resource pooling, and more.\n\nNOTE: This library is in very early stages. Additional features and types are planned for the 1.0 release.",
